ed (generator, n), n = 50–75 (six (generator, n) pairs with three to five ratios each)\n6750:### (d) Calibrated on the m = n ridge, predicted at the other ratios (19 series; the 13 at m ≤ n / 2 are the deciding ones)\n6787:### (e) What the excess is, and what it is not\n6818:### (f) The literature's transition is not the ridge\n6838:### (g) The ridge's height scales with m, steeply\n6874:**Size range covered.** Peaks and predictions at `n ∈ {50, 60, 75}`, `m / n\n6886:**Kill criterion.** None stated by the plan. Deliverable as asked: the ridge\n6913:(578 lines, 32 theorems, 3 `sorry`), `learning/sandwich.py`. Regenerate:*\n6917:python -m learning.sandwich                 # brute force to n = 5, corpus recount, lake build + #print axioms; 5 s\n6918:python -m pytest tests/test_sandwich.py -q  # 7 tests\n6934:### (a) What was defined\n6956:### (b) What was proved (no `sorry`, standard axioms only)\n7005:### (c) Do the definitions compute the right thing?\n7036:### (d) The corpus recount\n7050:The 2,823 is §5's \"ends coincide and force the optimum on 2,823\", regenerated.\n7059:### (e) Stated with `sorry`: the gap list\n7103:### (f) What the proofs do and do not cover\n7139:**Size range covered.** The theorems: every finite simple graph. The\n7144:**Kill criterion.** None stated by the plan. Deliverable as asked: two","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
