{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XQQ6Mpb4Ls8Ct2WrbHP9vh","type":"tool_result","content":"Sat Sep 26 08:24:04 PM WEST 2026\n# Kept separate from the project's requirements.txt on purpose: the solver does\n# not depend on any of this, and nothing in `learning/` is on its critical path.\npandas\nscikit-learn\nlightgbm\n# Optional, behind a soft import in learning/canonical.py: exact canonical forms\n# of the MOSP graph. Without it the module falls back to WL hashes alone.\npynauty\n# Optional, behind a soft import in learning/fingerprint.py: the 2-D map of\n# instance space. Without it the module falls back to PCA.\numap-learn\n# Optional, behind a soft import in learning/bound_gap.py: the explainable\n# boosting machine beside the depth-3 tree. Without it the EBM rows are skipped.\ninterpret-core\n# Optional, behind a soft import in learning/formula_search.py: symbolic\n# regression (bootstraps Julia on first use). Without it the enumerated search\n# runs alone and the PySR section of the tables says so.\npysr\n=====\n21:learning/data/*\n22:!learning/data/ensemble/\n25:learning/data/ensemble/recover_solutions/\n26:learning/models/\n32:learning/data/proofs/\n33:!learning/data/proofs.csv\n41:!learning/data/proofs_200k.csv\n44:learning/data/conjecture/\n47:learning/data/set_imitation/\n=====\n49e549fb Ralph loop0003 iteration 6: 06 · §2.5a Fan order. Behind a flag defaulting to today's behaviour,\n0eb33915 Fix the C better_move: a wrong close count, a cross-rule cycle, and a flag that hid both\nd3b060c8 Fix a false-refutation bug in better_move; one corpus optimum was wrong\n7e08dc8b Profile the C inner loop: the dominance rules are the inner loop\nc6eaa9b9 Port old move to C and turn it on: 1.6 to 2.6x, everywhere\n=====\n## 7. The second one, 2026-09-26: two bugs, neither the diagnosed one\n\n`reports/ml_nature.md` §15 ran the differential harness and found the C with\n`better_move` on answering `unsat` at the optimum on 56 of 17,527 sparse\ninstances at 10–40 customers (88 false answers), and diagnosed a cross-rule\ncycle: `better_move` discards `r` citing `q`, then `subset_rule` discards `q`\nciting `r`. That cycle is real — it is the whole story on the 10 × 13 minimal\ninstance — but the section's control, \"`better_move` alone is sound on all\n88\", was vacuous: the filter's early exit read\n`if (!subset_rule && !definite_move) goto sorted;`, so with the other two\nrules off `better_move` never ran (node counts identical to `better_move=False`,\n7 / 6 / 183 on the three test instances). Run genuinely alone it refutes the\n17 × 9 minimal instance at its optimum of 5.\n\n**Bug A, inside the rule.** `close(q, S ∪ {r})` was counted over every customer\nnot yet closed after `r`, including those `r` finishes on its own — customers\nwith nothing left to open, which the child node closes as free moves before\n`q` is ever played. Theorem 1's proof needs stacks closed *in addition* to\nthose. `definite_move` and `subset_rule` never counted them (their `ids` skip\nsize-0 customers); `better_move`, with no Python side, did. At the root of the\n17 × 9 instance, `1` pruned `2` with `closed_by = 2 ≥ opened_by = 2`, the two\nbeing `1` itself and `8`, whose whole neighbourhood sits inside `N[2]`.\n\n**Bug B, between rules.** As §15 said: `subset_rule` ran after `better_move`\nand measured survivors against every remaining customer, discarded candidates\nincluded.\n\n**Bug C, the flag.** The early exit above.\n\n### What the theorem needs in this search's cost model\n\nThe paper's open-stack count after playing a set is a function of the set;\nthis search closes free moves automatically, so its cost of `c` after closed\nset `C` is `|O(C ∪ {c})| − |C|`, which depends on `C` and not only on\n`C ∪ {c}`. Theorem 2's proof plays `q` first and `r` second, and the cost of\nthat second move is `|O(C) ∪ N(q) ∪ N(r)| − |fin(O(C) ∪ N(q))|`, which the\npaper's playability quantity `|O(C) ∪ N(r) ∪ N(q)| − |C| − 1` bounds from\nabove. So the \"inexact\" playability check the C already made is the right one,\nand making it exact — subtracting `r`'s free moves — would be wrong. Brute\nforce over every reachable state, every `k` and every ordered candidate pair\n=====\n49\nlearning/data/:\nbound_gap.csv\ncanonical.csv\nconjecture\ndegeneracy.csv\ndegeneracy_solutions\ndescent_bench.json\ndescent_bench_random.json\ndifferential_partial.csv\ndifferential_run.log\ndistil.csv\nensemble\nextremal\nguided_search.json\ninstance_space.csv\ninstances.csv\nnode_counts.csv\nproofs\nproofs.csv\nproofs_200k.csv\nproofs_200k_run.log\nproofs_retry_run.log\nproofs_run.log\nrace_corpus.json\nrace_dense.json\nrace_sparse.json\nrace_sweep.json\nset_imitation\nsweep_cs-dfs.json\nsweep_learned.json\nsweep_learned_cs-dfs.json\nsweep_ledger.csv\ntheorem2_partial.csv\n\nlearning/data/ensemble:\nconjecture_attack.csv\nconjecture_attack.log\nconjecture_attack_large.csv\nconjecture_attack_large.log\nconjecture_candidates.csv\nconjecture_chain.log\nconjecture_counterexamples.csv\nconjecture_counterexamples_large.csv\nconjecture_invariants.csv.gz\nconjecture_run.log\ncost_model_predictions.csv\ncost_model_recertify.csv\ndifferential.csv.gz\ndifferential_drawn.csv\ndifferential_drawn_rules.csv\ndifferential_summary.csv\nextremal_best.csv\nextremal_core10_run.log\nextremal_core_run.log\nextremal_corpus_run.log\nextremal_corpus_tw.csv\nextremal_jobs_core.csv\nextremal_jobs_core10.csv\nextremal_jobs_main.csv\nextremal_jobs_minimal.csv\nextremal_jobs_pilot.csv\nextremal_minimal_run.log\nextremal_search_run.log\nextremal_trace_core.csv.gz\nextremal_trace_core10.csv.gz\nextremal_trace_main.csv.gz\nextremal_trace_minimal.csv.gz\nextremal_trace_pilot.csv.gz\nfan_order.csv.gz\nfan_order_run.log\nmanifest.csv\nmanifest_ratio.csv\nmanifest_upward.csv\nportfolio.csv.gz\nportfolio_race.csv\nportfolio_race.log\nportfolio_run.log\nratio_run.log\nrecover.csv.gz\nrecover_lattice.csv\n82M\tlearning/data/ensemble\n52:    Yanass